cousin  welcome to the cookout the greatest  gathering of black family and food of  all time  if you get an invite to the cookout  whatever you bring has to be fire  because if it's not that chicken ain't  going to be the only thing getting  roasted so i'm going to show you how to  make some staples of the cookout like  uncle rome's barbecue grandma's macaroni  and cheese or unclear sweet potatoes but  today we're starting with an absolute  classic potato salad potato salad seems  simple but it's real easy to mess up now  if you stick with me i'll show you how  to make some potato salad ain't gonna  sit on the table i'm jermaine rawlings  and i'm inviting you to the cookout so  for black people potato salad is a sense  of nostalgia we literally want what our  grandmother made growing up so don't get  cute i use yukon gold potatoes because  they have a very thin skin and i don't  like peeling potatoes because ain't  nobody got time for that you want to  start with cold water and you add the  potatoes too and then bring it to a boil  all right so it's very important to  season your potatoes before the potato  salad is done i use chicken bouillon i  use this with my mashed potatoes i use  this when i'm making pasta because it  gives it a such a more robust flavor and  if you're vegetarian you can use veggie  bouillon and now we're going to stir  this up need a spoon  we're going to bring this up to a boil  let it go for about 15 minutes or until  it's fork tender then i'll strain it and  we'll be right back all right so  potatoes are done i checked them earlier  they were fork tender now it's time to  chop when you're chopping the potatoes  you want to make sure that the pieces  aren't too big or too small people don't  like to eat a full potato with one bite  so chop them up a little bit so that way  they fit on a fork you also don't want  to make them too small because then it  becomes mashed potato salad when you're  mixing it up in a bowl and nobody wants  that the perfect size for the potato  salad is kind of like a pineapple tidbit  just like that as you're cutting you'll  notice some of the peels are coming away  it doesn't really matter it's going to  get mixed up in the bowl anyway so don't  trip that is all our potatoes and now  we're going to move on to  the celery when you're cutting the  celery you want to make sure you get in  very small pieces because once again  nobody likes a chunky potato salad so i  always cut the half and the other half  so that in some places it's called a  quarter i usually go for celery because  i like the texture so it gives you a  little bit of crunch but not too much  crunch and then also like the flavor  just just goes with it and once again  that's what my grandma did celery is  pretty much one of the only vegetables  you want to put in there you don't want  to start putting carrots no raisins no  capers no olives because our  grandparents were not eating those in  their potatoes some people are scared to  use a sharp knife they think it's  dangerous but it's actually dangerous to  use a dull knife so make sure your knife  is sharp and just be careful keep your  eye on what you're doing okay so we're  going to add this to the bowl next we  have hard-boiled eggs boiled eggs is the  only protein you want to add to your  potato salad don't get cute once again  and add smoked salmon as much as i love  bacon a lot of black people don't eat  pork we don't do the whole swine and  dining type thing leave bacon out of it  cause this ain't for you it's for  everybody with the eggs i just give them  a quick chop nothing real precise just  make sure they're they're small enough  to evenly distribute and people like to  have the eggs in there so you want to  make sure they get some so don't put big  old chunks and then you only got three  people with egg eggs in their potato  salad now we're just giving it another  quick chop make sure there's no big  chunks and then we add these to the bowl  all right so onions some people like red  onions some people like brown onions but  for this you want a sweet onion because  it's a milder onion taste depending on  the cookout it might be some people  there that you might want to holla at  you don't want your breath smelling like  onion so you get the sweet onion so that  way it's not as strong and then also  what i do is i grate the onion so that  way you don't have chunks of onion  in the potato salad so before you grate  it you want to cut the onion in half  because i'm only going to use half this  onion by the way take that part off and  then grab it and you're going to grate  it over top  it's almost like you're juicing your  onion we all like onion juice right when  you're grating your onion be careful  because you can lose some skin on them  knuckles if you slip up so i'm crying  little thug tears because this potato  salad will be so good all right we're  done grating onions and as you can see  our balls getting a little full five  pounds of potatoes so uh i'm going to  get a bigger bowl and the ingredients  for our mayo mixture see you guys in a  second all right folks now we're ready  for one of the most important parts the  mayo mixture some people like mayo some  people don't i like mayo in my salad as  well as mustard for this particular  recipe i use half miracle whip and half  mayo some people might be like well  you're just doing too much growing up  and to this day it's kind of like craig  i have like kool-aid no sugar sometimes  peanut butter no jelly ham no burger i  had a little bit of mayo and i had a  little bit of miracle whip when i was  developing the recipe so i just use both  we're gonna add the miracle whip  we're gonna add the mayo  and then we have some dijon mustard and  i like coarse stone ground mustard  because i'm bougie now because you know  i made it you know what i'm saying also  i add hot sauce this right here is  actually frank's because you can get it  everywhere but some people prefer other  hot sauces the hot sauce and the ground  mustard will give it a little bit of  kick it's five pounds of potato so it  won't be too much so don't be scared  worst case scenario you'll need to put  hot sauce in it because you know most  people got it in a bag all right you  always want to make sure you're mixing  this up in a separate bowl because you  don't want to like overwork the potatoes  because then that's how to get mashed  and they get all weird and then it'll  sit on the table and then i'm going to  add in the garlic powder if you grew up  in a black household then you know  everything gets garlic powder onion  powder paprika so mayo mixture is done  now we're going to add everything  together and mix it up all right so now  we're going to add the relish this is  dill relish and then we have the sweet  relish now some might ask why are you  using sweet relish and i told you a  little story about the miracle whip in  the mail same situation also the dill  gives it a little bit of the savory and  then you have the sweet now once you  have everything together you're going to  mix it up again be careful because you  don't want to like mash the potatoes  just give it you know like a little  little mix don't try to get trendy and  like add cheese and all that stuff just  just keep it keep it traditional like  i'm pushing it with the stone ground  mustard to be honest now this this is  looking pretty good i'm just to be  honest with you this ain't going to last  very long that's why i get 5 pounds of  potato all right we got this all mixed  up and we're going to put it in a better  bowl because you don't want to show up  with this bowl if you ever been to the  cookout you know presentation is  everything so you need your garnish so  put a little fresh cracked pepper on  there  you put a little paprika need that  you need the paprika if you think you  put a little bit too much just put a  little bit more with this potato salad  without the paprika on top you need that  a little bit of celery seed and then  some fresh chives don't go getting fancy  adding some tarragon or dill you got  dill from the pickles  and nobody likes licorice so don't put  tarragon in there just a little bit of  chive or  green onion just you know keep it keep  it simple i like my potato salad cold  like every other black person so we're  gonna put this in the refrigerator for a  little bit and then we're gonna have  some people from the cookout try it out  but while we wait i was curious to know  what other ingredients people hate to  see in the potato salad so i sent a team  around tasty to find out let's see what  they came up with what's up tasty  jermaine just led you through everything  that you should do when making the  perfect potato salad but we think it  remains to be said there are some things  that you should absolutely not do as  well so we're gonna go around and taste  the office and see what the good people  have to say name one thing that should  never go in potato salad raisins  no raisins raisins  has anyone said raisins yes raisins i  mean being this black history month the  first thing i got to say is we got to  stop gentrifying recipes as well raisins  leave the raisins out of your potato  salad please for all potlucks  all cookouts all everything no raisins  but make sure the potatoes is firm it  got the skin on them none of that mashed  potato stuff in my potato salad i want  to hear i want that crunch that good  yeah i'm saying yeah all that  no raisins though we're not doing that  raisin stuff yeah so raisins that's a  no-go so pretty much any fruit that  isn't a potato shouldn't be in there  wait wait  you get what i'm saying right no  luckily none of that stuff is in here  but don't take my word for it let's let  the homies try it out  the ratio of mayonnaise so everything  else is great approved  [Music]  not a single raisin approved  this does not bring this onto our  ancestors approved well there you have  it that's how you make potato salad  worthy of the cookout so tell me in the  comments what this you want to bring to  the cookout and maybe i'll tell you how  to make it i'm about to go take a walk  around the corner with my cousins but  always remember no raisins i'm jamae  rawlings peace  oh yes  [Music]  you

